    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lead-Executive--Communications----Communication---Outreach-Department_JR-10000055790": {
      "title": "Lead Executive (Communications) - Communication & Outreach Department",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are looking for a strategic web and communications professional to strengthen NYP’s brand through creative storytelling and impactful digital communications campaigns. You will manage and create content across websites and digital platforms, support external communications, and work closely with departments to shape clear and compelling narratives to enhance audience engagement and communications outcomes. [What you will be working on] Manage NYP websites, ensuring content is clear, well‑organised and user‑friendly, while improving discoverability across search engines and AI-driven platforms through SEO and GEO best practices. Work closely with stakeholders to understand their needs, identify opportunities and translate them into effective web solutions, ensuring content structure and user journeys support intended business outcomes. Implement data tracking and set performance metrics to monitor web and campaign outcomes. Conduct research and analyse audience data to uncover insights, identify trends, and inform future communications strategies. Craft compelling content through impactful copywriting and storytelling across the NYP website and digital platforms such as online articles and eDMs. Ensure all messaging is consistent, relevant to target segments, and aligned with NYP’s brand voice. Support internal and external communications efforts across NYP, including developing communications plans for departments, assisting with media enquiries, and ensuring consistent alignment with NYP's brand voice and communications strategy. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualifications in Communications, Marketing or relevant disciplines. At least 3 to 5 years of relevant working experience in website management, content creation, communications, or marketing communications. Experience in website content management, with a good understanding of content structure and SEO fundamentals to enhance user experience, discoverability, and engagement. Knowledge Flair for writing with the ability to craft engaging content across multiple platforms. Solid understanding of government or institutional website platforms such as Isomer, as well as understanding of SEO principles and experience using tools such as Google Analytics to guide content strategy and measure performance is an advantage. Knowledge of internal communications best practices and experience supporting departmental communications planning is an advantage. Familiarity with media relations practices, including drafting media releases, managing media enquiries, and understanding the media landscape. Skills Excellent copywriting and editing ability across a range of formats including media releases, speeches, web copy, and editorial content. Experience in content creation and editing across different formats, including written content, visuals (e.g. posters), and/or video. Strong project management skills, with the ability to manage timelines, stakeholders, and multiple priorities effectively. Strong interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate and communicate effectively with various stakeholders. Attributes Self-motivated with a strong sense of initiative, and a collaborative team player. Able to manage multiple tasks effectively, work under pressure, and meet tight deadlines. Demonstrates sound judgment, strong analytical thinking, and effective problem-solving skills to make timely and well-reasoned decisions. #LI-Onsite"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Deputy-Manager-Manager---Admissions-and-Academic-Affairs-Department_JR-10000055863": {
      "title": "Deputy Manager/Manager - Admissions and Academic Affairs Department",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will be leading data-driven initiatives, support strategic decision-making across student admissions and academic administration, and strengthen system capabilities. [What you will be working on] Leads and oversees a team responsible for data management, reporting and analytics, digital transformation, and systems enhancement initiatives. Partners stakeholders across the Polytechnic to leverage data, streamline operational processes, and deliver digital solutions that enhance efficiency, governance, and user experience. Manages and enhances admissions, enrolment, and academic-related systems. Lead and manage CET learners' administration operations, including offer management and academic related matters Leads and contributes to digital transformation initiatives that enhance service delivery and learners’ experience, including the development of e-workflows and process automation solutions using tools such as Microsoft Power Apps Designs and develops dashboards and reports to support admissions, enrolment, and academic operations. Leverages digital tools to generate accurate and meaningful statistics covering admissions, enrolment, academic performance, and student-related data, to analyse trends and patterns to provide actionable insights for management decision-making. Support institutional reporting requirements and data submissions to external agencies. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualifications in Information Systems, Computer Science, Data Analytics, Statistics, Business Analytics, or a related discipline. At least 3 years of relevant experience in systems administration, data management and analytics, digital transformation, or project management. Experience in leading teams in projects and engaging stakeholders across multiple functions. Proficient in data visualisation and reporting tools such as Power BI, Excel, or equivalent platforms. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to translate data into actionable insights. Familiarity with SQL and business process improvement methodologies, and experience in the education or public sector environment will be an added advantage. A team player with a positive attitude and strong leadership potential, with excellent stakeholder management, communication, and project management skills. #LI-Onsite"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Executive-Senior-Executive---Eco-Campus-Solutions---Services-Dept_JR-10000055891": {
      "title": "Executive/Senior Executive - Eco-Campus Solutions & Services Dept",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Join a team of facilities management practitioners and work closely with the team on the implementation of workplace transformation efforts within the department. [What you will be working on] Contribute to the transformation strategy by supporting the team's transition towards AI adoption and digitalization efforts within ESS .   Take on the transformational AI and digitalization projects within ESS. You will work with project teams (internal/external), engage in problem-solving exercises, engage in the implementation of monitoring dashboards and be responsible for the accuracy, efficiency, explainability, performance and scalability of the AI and digitalization solutions.   Collaborate with cross-functional teams of engineers, managers and domain experts to deliver timely AI / digitalization solutions for facilities operations and space management ensuring strong documentation and record-management standards within the team.   Develop AI/digitalization solutions with service providers that enhances facilities operations and space optimization and maintain analytic tools, dashboard reporting and processes that aid in data-driven decision making.   Undertake other responsibilities as assigned to support ESS’s transformation efforts . [What we are looking for] Good interpersonal, leadership and communication (verbal & written) skills. Data analytic or relevant IT knowledge."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer--Sociology--Psychology---Lifeskills----Sch-of-Health---Social-Sciences_JR-10000055995": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Sociology, Psychology & Lifeskills) - Sch of Health & Social Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will be working in the School of Health & Social Sciences to plan, develop and teach sociology as the main discipline, while also contributing to the teaching of psychology and lifeskills-related modules for Pre-Employment Training (PET) and/or Continuing Education and Training (CET). [What you will be working on] Develop and/or conduct lessons (e.g., lectures, tutorials, seminars, project supervision, etc.) in sociology, psychology, and lifeskills-related subjects (e.g., research, critical thinking, innovation, communication, interpersonal & collaboration skills, etc.) for Pre-Employment Training (PET) or Continuing Education and Training (CET) learners, particularly in the health and social sciences domain. Undertake assigned student mentoring, including accompanying students for overseas educational/exchange trips. Contribute to school promotional activities, administrative functions, and committee work, particularly those requiring expertise in sociology, psychology, research methods, data analysis, or social science-related fields. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Sociology, Psychology, or a closely related Social Science discipline preferably with at least 3 years of relevant work experience. Additional qualification in communication and/or other-lifeskills related competency would be an advantage as would working experience in health & social care and/or educational settings. Proficient in IT applications, including familiarity with AI tools, for administration, teaching & learning and research & data analysis. Analytical and meticulous individual who can think strategically and align with NYP and the national agenda. People-oriented individual who possesses strong interpersonal, communication and presentation skills, including the capacity to work well in cross-functional teams."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/NYP-FN/Senior-Executive---Finance-Department_JR-10000056055": {
      "title": "Senior Executive - Finance Department",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Responsible for project code setup and budgeting, preparation of financial statements, journals, and payment documentation, including grant drawdowns and internal charges. Conduct annual stocktakes and support operational and financial processes. [What you will be working on] Manage project code creation and budgeting Prepare financial statement for month-end, quarter-end, and year-end Prepare and process journals for month-end, quarter-end, and year-end including grant drawdown and internal charge Process payment documentation for NETS machine charges Conduct annual stocktakes to ensure inventory accuracy Provide other operational and financial processes #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Accounting and financial reporting knowledge Experience in journal preparation and period-end closing Budgeting and project code administration Proficient in Microsoft Excel and financial system Strong analytical, organizational, and communication skills Meticulous with good attention to detail and ability to meet deadlines"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Snr-Lecturer--AI-Augmented-Product-Architect--Sch-of-Engineeering_JR-10000051317": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Snr Lecturer (AI-Augmented Product Architect)-Sch of Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Nanyang Polytechnic is seeking a dynamic and experienced Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in AI-Augmented Product Architecture to contribute to our School of Engineering. This role involves teaching and mentoring students across both PET (Diploma) and CET (Adult Learning) programmes using modern pedagogical approaches, curriculum development in emerging technology domains, industry engagement, applied research, and academic administration. [What you will be working on] Instructional Delivery & Facilitation Deliver lectures, tutorials and laboratory sessions across full-time Diploma programs (PET) and adult workforce upskilling modules (CET). Adopt diversified pedagogical frameworks, including project-based learning, flipped classrooms, and blended e-learning spaces. Supervise and mentor students during final-year projects, multi-disciplinary capstone assignments, and professional internship placements, particularly in Edge AI, IoT systems, and distributed architectures. Curriculum Design & Development Design, review, and revitalize instructional resources, module structures, and assessment rubrics aligned to emerging industry practices in Edge AI and distributed systems. Embed competencies such as AI model optimization and edge analytics into curriculum delivery. Develop hands-on lab modules involving embedded AI deployment, IoT telemetry pipelines, and hardware acceleration platforms. Industry Engagement & Applied Research Establish partnerships with industry players in Edge AI, IoT, and smart infrastructure. Contribute to applied R&D and industry partnership in areas such as edge AI, digital twin systems can smart connected systems. Translate real-world deployments (e.g., edge inference, chiller optimisation, smart monitoring) into learning case studies. Student Development & Administrative Duties Mentor students in technical and career development within Edge AI and embedded systems domains. Perform academic administration duties including assessment tracking and quality assurance. #LI-Hybrid [What we are looking for] Education: Degree or Postgraduate qualification in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Information Systems, or related fields. Industry Experience: Minimum 3–5 years in software development, AI application development, or product engineering. (Candidate should demonstrate strong proficiency in at least 2 of the following areas)     i.    AI-Augmented Development & Low-Code/No-Code Experience with low-code/no-code and AI-assisted (“vibe coding”) tools to rapidly prototype web, mobile, and backend applications.     ii.    Agentic AI & Workflow Orchestration Understanding of agentic AI concepts (reasoning, tool use, multi-step workflows) and ability to build agent-driven applications integrated with APIs or IoT systems.     iii.   LLM Deployment (Cloud & Edge) Familiarity with deploying LLMs via cloud and/or edge (SLMs), including integration into applications and trade-offs (latency, cost, privacy).     iv.   Cross-Platform Application Development Experience in building web and cross-OS mobile apps (iOS & Android) using frameworks such as Flutter or React Native, with simple, user-centric UI design.     v.    AI Application Security & Risk Awareness Awareness of risks (e.g., prompt injection, data leakage, API vulnerabilities) and basic practices in secure AI application design and governance."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/NYP/Senior-Executive--Social-Work-_JR-10000053360": {
      "title": "Senior Executive (Social Work)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will be working with the School of Health and Social Sciences supporting the social work section on the administrative work and also on other industry-related work. [What you will be working on] Social Work Course advising to prospective learners Social Media marketing of courses Lead or support in school-level or course-related events such as pre-placement workshops, orientation programme, Open House activities, Alumni events, Overseas Student exchanges and Study Trips Support and maintain course and placement database Support administration of course applications, procurement and facilities bookings [What we are looking for] Diploma in any field (preferably in Social Work or a related discipline) At least 3 years of relevant work experience, including programme and event management Good team player with strong communication and interpersonal skills Service-oriented mindset in supporting academic and operational stakeholders Ability to manage multiple operational tasks concurrently with minimal supervision Proficient in Microsoft Excel, and other Microsoft applications Strong administrative skills with a proven track record of managing administrative and procurement processes effectively"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Executive--CET-Admin----School-of-Design---Media_JR-10000052988": {
      "title": "Executive (CET Admin) - School of Design & Media",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] This role provides operational administrative support for the delivery of short courses under Continuing Education and Training (CET). The candidate will support course setup in the course management system, participant onboarding, attendance administration, and day-to-day course logistics to ensure each course run is delivered smoothly and accurately. Working closely with course teams and trainers, the candidate will coordinate trainer availability, manage the course calendar and room bookings, and handle on-site arrangements such as materials and refreshments. The work follows well-defined procedures, with scope to contribute to process improvements at the project level. This role is ideal for someone who is organised, detail-oriented, and enjoys keeping operations running smoothly, while building familiarity with CET administration and training funding requirements. [What you will be working on] Key Responsibilities: Set up short courses and intakes in the course management system (STEP) according to established procedures, maintaining accurate course, schedule, and trainer records, and managing the master course calendar and room bookings across runs. Process participant registration, onboarding, and enrolment confirmation, maintain participant data and supporting documents for compliance, and set up participant network access (guest WiFi) accounts where required. Administer attendance taking, tracking, and certification for each course run, and compile attendance and completion reports to support training funding and claim submissions. Coordinate refreshment ordering and venue readiness, liaising with vendors and ensuring training rooms and equipment are prepared ahead of each session. Coordinate with trainers and associate trainers to confirm availability, and process associate trainer claims and timesheets in line with established procedures. Respond to participant, trainer, and public enquiries (including MySkillsFuture), escalating non-standard cases, and administer post-course feedback surveys for funded and customised courses. Support course fee waiver requests by collating supporting documents and routing them for the required approvals. Maintain course run documents and records in the shared document system (SharePoint). [What we are looking for] Requirements: Experience in administrative or operations support, ideally within a training, education, or adult learning environment. Comfortable learning and working with structured systems and procedures, and able to pick up new course administration platforms quickly. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage attendance, records, and scheduling accurately and on time. Attention to detail in maintaining participant data and supporting documents for compliance and funding requirements. Good communication skills to liaise with participants, trainers, and vendors with tact and diplomacy. Collaborative and proactive, able to work within well-defined procedures while supporting smooth day-to-day operations. Prior experience in Continuing Education and Training (CET) administration, familiarity with SkillsFuture Singapore (SSG) funding and processes, or hands-on knowledge of the STEP course management system would be an advantage."
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer--Business-Digitalisation----School-of-Business-Management_JR-10000053797": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Business Digitalisation) – School of Business Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are looking for professionals who can teach students how to think alongside AI tools, not just how to use them — developing adaptive analytical thinking that transfers across tools and contexts, and helping learners understand when to trust AI outputs, when to override them, and how to combine human judgment with machine capability. [What you will be working on] Design and deliver Data Analytics and Business Analytics programmes covering data literacy, data visualisation, business intelligence, predictive analytics, AI applications, and modern data platforms using tools such as Excel, Power BI, Python, and SQL. Teach predictive analytics and forecasting techniques, including machine learning, clustering, dimension reduction, and time-series analysis, using Python and industry-standard analytics libraries. Guide learners in developing data-driven solutions and lightweight application prototypes while building business analysis and project management capabilities. Integrate machine learning, generative AI, and agentic AI into teaching, enabling learners to apply AI technologies effectively, responsibly, and critically. Develop and deliver continuing education and professional development programmes that strengthen analytics and AI capabilities for working professionals. Design authentic learning activities and assessments that evaluate analytical reasoning, problem-solving, human judgment, and responsible AI usage. Develop, review, and enhance curriculum, learning materials, laboratories, and assessments, including the adoption of Python-based tools and workflows across programmes. Stay abreast of developments in analytics, AI, and emerging technologies, translating industry practices into relevant and current teaching content. Work closely with academic teams, industry partners, and stakeholders to ensure curriculum relevance and alignment with workforce needs. Provide student mentorship, pastoral care, career guidance, and internship support to nurture learners' professional growth. Participate in outreach, industry engagement, and recruitment activities to promote data literacy, analytics, AI capabilities, and the School's programmes. Support internationalisation efforts, including overseas learning programmes, study trips, and collaborative educational initiatives. Teach and engage both full-time and adult learners, adapting pedagogical approaches to diverse learner profiles and experience levels. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Data Science, Business Analytics, Statistics, Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related discipline (or Education with a strong analytics/technology focus). Minimum 3 years of relevant experience in analytics, training delivery, or professional development within technology, education, corporate, or public-sector contexts. Strong analytics capability, with experience in data preparation, analysis, modelling, and translating insights into business decisions. Proficiency in Python for analytics and machine learning, including predictive modelling, clustering, dimension reduction, forecasting, and model evaluation. Ability to develop and teach lightweight Python web applications with SQL database integration. Strong proficiency in Excel and business intelligence tools (e.g. Power BI, Tableau); exposure to modern data platforms such as Databricks is a plus. Working knowledge of machine learning, generative AI, and agentic AI, with the ability to teach concepts and guide responsible AI adoption. Familiarity with GenAI tools (e.g. ChatGPT, Claude, Microsoft Copilot) and AI ethics and governance principles. Experience with Microsoft Power Platform and Microsoft 365 technologies is an advantage. Ability to teach technical concepts to non-technical audiences and translate complex analytics and AI topics into practical learning experiences. Strong communication, stakeholder management, and collaboration skills. Relevant experience in one or more of the following areas is preferred: End-to-end analytics projects, from problem framing and data preparation to analysis, visualisation, and insight communication. Designing or supervising AI-assisted or agentic analytical workflows Implementing business intelligence or automation solutions in an organisational setting Teaching or coaching with generative AI, including designing assessments that remain valid when learners have AI assistance Building a portfolio of analytics or application projects (e.g. GitHub repositories, published notebooks)"
    },
    "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Nanyang-Polytechnic/Lecturer-Snr-Lecturer--Biologics---Process-Technology--Sch-of-Applied-Science_JR-10000054002": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Snr Lecturer (Biologics & Process Technology)-Sch of Applied Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will be playing an active role in the academic, professional, and personal development of the learners to prepare them for work and life. This includes development of Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education & Training (CET) curriculums, programme delivery and working on industry projects. [What you will be working on] Develop course including curriculum development, course delivery (face-to-face & online) and project supervision. Prepare and grade assessments and supervise learners in their daily course work. Manage Learning Management System (LMS), execute interactive digital tools (e.g. Kahoot, Mentimeter) and harness technology to enhance teaching and learning. Be Personal Mentor to learners, support them in pastoral care and handle day-to-day administrative matters. Support the school’s strategic initiatives through involvement in committee work and projects. Spearhead and identify new opportunities, initiatives, and collaborations with the industry. Manage and undertake project development with industry. [What we are looking for] Highly motivated and resourceful candidates who are nurturing and enjoy interacting with learners with the following: At least 3 years of relevant work experience in biologics manufacturing related field, especially upstream and/or downstream processing . Relevant qualifications in science or chemical engineering. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Proficient in digital skills (including the use of AI and data analytics tools), ability to adapt and multi-task. Candidates are also expected to be involved in the teaching and curriculum development of areas such as: Biologics Upstream or Downstream Operations AI or Digital Skills for Process Industry Data & Statistical Methods It will be an advantage if the candidates have relevant experience and are proficient in analytics tools (e.g. Microsoft Power BI, Tableau). #LI-Hybrid"
    }
  },
